      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s second sentence adds that the pitch differences “can matter for understanding how sounds are perceived,” which is not stated in the packet. The packet instead describes individual differences in pitch apprehension (diplacusis) and notes it may have “pathological import,” and separately notes other binaural hearing phenomena as “of importance for the theory of audition,” but it does not support the specific claim about understanding sound perception."
